1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,456
Every evening, in millions of kitchens,
the same question… what's for dinner?

2
00:00:06,706 --> 00:00:11,117
This is Sous, keeping everyone at the
table safe.

3
00:00:11,967 --> 00:00:20,897
Up to 40% of America's food is wasted… and
1 in 13 kids has a food allergy.

4
00:00:23,547 --> 00:00:27,101
Tell Sous once: Grandpa needs low sodium…

5
00:00:27,141 --> 00:00:31,552
and it applies to every meal from now on.

6
00:00:32,802 --> 00:00:37,847
What should we cook tonight? Recipes
ranked by what expires first.

7
00:00:37,887 --> 00:00:44,043
Peanut noodles out for Leo… salty fried
rice set aside for Grandpa.

8
00:00:45,193 --> 00:00:48,285
Out of eggs? Sous suggests swaps…

9
00:00:48,325 --> 00:00:53,661
and drops any that clash with an allergy
at the table.

10
00:00:54,211 --> 00:00:57,697
Plan dinners for the next three nights.

11
00:00:59,947 --> 00:01:07,490
One sentence, three MCP tool calls…
suggest, save the plan, build the cart.

12
00:01:08,540 --> 00:01:15,620
Nothing is bought until I say yes… and the
order goes through exactly once.

13
00:01:16,870 --> 00:01:23,593
Now we cook, hands-free, every step big
enough to read across the room.

14
00:01:25,443 --> 00:01:29,854
When a step needs time, Sous offers a
timer.

15
00:01:31,804 --> 00:01:39,809
Hands busy? I tap Next instead… voice and
touch call the same MCP tools.

16
00:01:40,259 --> 00:01:44,208
Every step stays on screen, ingredients
ticked off.

17
00:01:45,558 --> 00:01:51,161
Dinner's ready… $6.79 of food, saved from
the bin.

18
00:01:51,201 --> 00:01:54,121
Then… Leo's lips start swelling.

19
00:01:54,371 --> 00:01:55,718
Sous doesn't guess.

20
00:01:55,758 --> 00:02:02,548
A fixed script, checked before anything
else: call 911, use his epinephrine…

21
00:02:02,588 --> 00:02:03,788
don't wait.

22
00:02:04,013 --> 00:02:05,822
On a tight budget?

23
00:02:05,862 --> 00:02:11,266
Sous finds the cheapest use-it-up dinners,
priced per serving…

24
00:02:11,306 --> 00:02:13,405
tonight's costs nothing extra.

25
00:02:14,555 --> 00:02:19,786
And what we won't use goes to a community
fridge…

26
00:02:22,036 --> 00:02:26,909
only after a yes, and it counts as food
rescued.

27
00:02:28,559 --> 00:02:37,952
$25 rescued this week, nearly 11 kg of CO₂
avoided… $1,300 a year.

28
00:02:39,102 --> 00:02:45,430
A brand-new session… and Sous still
remembers Leo's allergy and Grandpa's
diet.

29
00:02:45,470 --> 00:02:48,031
That's real memory, across sessions.

30
00:02:50,281 --> 00:02:55,050
Sous. Less waste… and everyone at the
table, safe.

